WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.744
The Contact Center reports are grouped into categories, and each category answers a

00:00:05.744 --> 00:00:07.503
different kind of question.

00:00:07.503 --> 00:00:11.661
This video walks through the categories with a real report from each, so

00:00:11.661 --> 00:00:13.580
you know which report to open.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.036
Executive is the one page for leaders.

00:00:21.036 --> 00:00:25.904
Operations and Queue and Routing show how calls and queues performed.

00:00:25.904 --> 00:00:28.500
Agent Performance looks at people.

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.366
Workforce and Payroll counts agents' time.

00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:35.417
Billing and Usage measures what was used.

00:00:35.417 --> 00:00:39.507
Compliance and Audit lists the records behind the totals.

00:00:39.507 --> 00:00:43.077
Technical and IT looks at providers and failures.

00:00:43.077 --> 00:00:48.400
CRM and Campaigns holds the reports of the CRM, which have their own videos.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:56.820
Executive has one report, the Executive performance dashboard.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:01:01.606
Cards show the main numbers, and charts show the daily trend, the channel

00:01:01.606 --> 00:01:06.090
mix, each queue's service level, and the agents with the most calls.

00:01:08.371 --> 00:01:10.150
It answers one question:

00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:11.811
is the center healthy?

00:01:11.811 --> 00:01:15.845
Open it first, and use its filters to look at one queue group,

00:01:15.845 --> 00:01:17.921
one channel or one direction.

00:01:22.192 --> 00:01:26.059
Operations shows how the center performed over time.

00:01:26.059 --> 00:01:29.660
Call insights gives the cards and a daily trend.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:37.262
Interaction volume trend and Interval performance show each day's outcomes, speed of answer and handle time.

00:01:37.762 --> 00:01:43.401
Hour-of-day performance and Day-of-week performance show when demand arrives.

00:01:43.401 --> 00:01:45.372
The hours are in U.T.C.

00:01:45.837 --> 00:01:55.488
Channel performance, Direction performance, Interaction outcome summary and Interaction lifecycle duration compare channels, directions and outcomes.

00:01:55.488 --> 00:02:00.407
Call quality shows how calls were rated, and where the poor ones cluster.

00:02:04.656 --> 00:02:07.110
Queue and Routing is about queues.

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:12.203
Queue service level shows, for each queue, the share of calls answered within

00:02:12.203 --> 00:02:14.534
the threshold set on that queue.

00:02:14.534 --> 00:02:20.976
Queue usage shows handled, answered and abandoned calls, handle time, and how many are waiting now.

00:02:21.431 --> 00:02:27.691
Queue abandonment analysis, Queue wait time analysis, Queue handle time analysis, Queue performance

00:02:27.691 --> 00:02:32.341
summary and Queue transfer performance each look at one side of a queue.

00:02:32.341 --> 00:02:35.381
Transfer analysis shows where transfers went.

00:02:35.381 --> 00:02:39.911
High-wait interaction detail lists calls that waited a minute or more.

00:02:40.402 --> 00:02:45.051
Agent availability and wait time and Dialer decision log are live reports.

00:02:45.051 --> 00:02:49.235
They explain why an agent is not getting calls, and why the dialer

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.862
did not call a record.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:57.780
Agent Performance compares people.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:05.400
Agent productivity shows each agent's handled calls, talk time, average handle time and completed activities.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:10.716
Agent utilization is busy plus wrap-up time divided by signed-in time.

00:03:10.716 --> 00:03:15.922
Agent occupancy divides it by the time the agent was available to take work.

00:03:15.922 --> 00:03:19.160
Both show how busy an agent is, not how good.

00:03:19.644 --> 00:03:26.298
Agent handle time analysis, Agent wrap-up performance, the inbound, outbound, transfer and outcome

00:03:26.298 --> 00:03:30.905
reports, and Talk, hold, ring and queue wait each look at one part

00:03:30.905 --> 00:03:32.504
of an agent's work.

00:03:36.714 --> 00:03:42.088
Workforce and Payroll reports count the time agents spend in each state.

00:03:42.088 --> 00:03:47.738
Agent time summary shows signed-in, available, busy, wrap-up and break time.

00:03:47.738 --> 00:03:51.114
Daily agent timecard breaks it down by day.

00:03:51.572 --> 00:03:57.104
Reconciled payroll timecard shows each agent's day beside the time in every state,

00:03:57.104 --> 00:04:00.058
and flags every day that does not add up.

00:04:00.058 --> 00:04:01.881
It shows time, not pay:

00:04:01.881 --> 00:04:04.772
pay rates and schedules are not applied.

00:04:05.225 --> 00:04:12.078
Presence status duration, Presence reason breakdown, Ready versus not-ready time, Agent break and

00:04:12.078 --> 00:04:18.797
away analysis, Queue signed-in hours and Campaign signed-in hours cut the same time other ways.

00:04:18.797 --> 00:04:21.525
All of them are limited to 31 days.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:29.242
Billing and Usage measures what the center used.

00:04:29.242 --> 00:04:37.370
Queue usage for billing lists each queue's interactions, connected time, wrap-up, queue wait, transfers and recordings.

00:04:37.821 --> 00:04:43.455
Agent, Channel, Provider and Daily usage for billing group the same measures by

00:04:43.455 --> 00:04:46.040
agent, channel, provider and day.

00:04:46.040 --> 00:04:49.155
They apply no prices, contracts or taxes:

00:04:49.155 --> 00:04:52.601
they support an invoice, they do not make one.

00:04:56.773 --> 00:05:01.334
Compliance and Audit lists the records behind the totals.

00:05:01.334 --> 00:05:09.153
Interaction detail has one row per interaction, with its queue, agent, provider, timing and transfers.

00:05:09.627 --> 00:05:15.178
Recording coverage shows how many answered voice calls have a recording, by provider.

00:05:15.178 --> 00:05:18.167
Agent recording coverage shows it by agent.

00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:24.581
Abandoned interaction detail and Long interaction detail list the calls behind those totals.

00:05:24.581 --> 00:05:29.868
Agent presence audit and Agent activity timeline list every state change and call

00:05:29.868 --> 00:05:31.995
change of an agent, in order.

00:05:36.199 --> 00:05:40.376
Technical and IT is for the people who run the phone system.

00:05:40.376 --> 00:05:45.819
Provider performance compares outcomes and durations by communications provider.

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:50.590
Call leg performance looks at each leg of a call, and Failed interaction

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:54.190
detail lists every call that failed for a technical reason.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:00.641
Is the center healthy this week?

00:06:00.641 --> 00:06:03.426
Open the Executive performance dashboard.

00:06:03.426 --> 00:06:05.499
Are callers waiting too long?

00:06:05.499 --> 00:06:09.410
Open Queue service level, then High-wait interaction detail.

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.695
Who needs coaching?

00:06:11.695 --> 00:06:15.441
Open Agent productivity and Agent handle time analysis.

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:18.204
Who was on the clock, and for how long?

00:06:18.204 --> 00:06:20.600
Open Reconciled payroll timecard.

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:23.236
Are calls being recorded?

00:06:23.236 --> 00:06:25.061
Open Recording coverage.

00:06:25.061 --> 00:06:26.765
Is a provider failing?

00:06:26.765 --> 00:06:30.660
Open Provider performance, then Failed interaction detail.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.691
Eight categories, one kind of question each.

00:06:35.691 --> 00:06:40.663
Start with the dashboard, then open the category that matches your question.

00:06:40.663 --> 00:06:42.240
Thanks for watching.

